  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HEADSTARTING THE GEOMETRIC TORTOISE (PSAMMOBATES GEOMETRICUS) TO SUSTAIN AND ENHANCE ITS LAST MAJOR POPULATION</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THIS PROJECT AIMS TO HELP CONSERVE THE REMAINING POPULATION OF THIS SPECIES, WHICH IS PERIODICALLY DECIMATED BY CATASTROPHIC FIRES THAT KILL LARGE NUMBERS OF TORTOISES. THIS REQUIRES REPOPULATING WITH HEAD-STARTED TURTLES AS NATURAL REPRODUCTION AND GROWTH IS SLOW. THIS SPECIES IS PARTICULARLY VULNERABLE TO EXTINCTION DUE TO ITS LIMITED REMAINING HABITAT IN SOUTH AFRICA, PERIODIC CATASTROPHIC FIRES, AND ITS INABILITY TO REPRODUCE IN CAPTIVITY. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) REPLANTING HERBACEOUS FYNBOS SPECIES THAT ARE EATEN BY OR PROVIDE SHELTER TO THIS TORTOISE (2) CONSTRUCTING ENCLOSURES TO HOUSE HEAD-STARTED TORTOISES (3) CONDUCTING FIELD SURVEYS TO DETERMINE THE POPULATION SIZE AND SURVIVAL RATES TO INFORM MANAGEMENT DECISIONS AND (4) CONDUCTING FIELD STUDIES TO DETERMINE DISTRIBUTION OF TORTOISE FOOD PLANTS AND TORTOISE MOVEMENTS TO PLAN EFFECTIVE TORTOISE RELEASES AND CONTROLLED BURNS.</narrative>
  </description>
